KNOWNBUG: [unique.ptr.single.ctor]/1 -- a default-constructed unique_ptr must
be null, but the constructor-template specialization
unique_ptr<C>::unique_ptr() is created with a nil body (the inline body is
never sourced from the member template of the lazily-completed class
instance), so the call is a silent no-op and the pointer stays nondet
(assertion currently FAILS).  Root of all unique_ptr value/delete-precondition
failures in cpp11_unique_ptr_member_enable_if.  Same deferred member-body
instantiation gap as the map/tuple "no body for callee" cases.  Flip to CORE
once member bodies are instantiated on odr-use.
